In re: the BATF's war on the Branch Davidians, not only will .50 caliber
machine guns penetrate the armored cars they're using, elephant guns loaded
with solids will penetrate the tanks, and up to 2.5 inches of steel.  They'd
better hope God's Marines never thought of that!

The BATFies who got killed deserved what they got.  No one can do such
work for long without forfeiting their humanity.

It's incorrect to call the Branch Davidians irrational.  They're perfectly
rational, given their premises.  They just have unsound premises, from which
they reason with all logical validity to outlandish conclusions.  This is
one of the reasons we all have reason to sympathize with them: many of our
premises are thought unsound by others, and the conclusions we draw seem
just as unreasonable - and, frankly, I think this claim is universal.

They believe in the Rapture, many of us believe in the nanotechnorapture.
Pascal had his wager, we have cryonics.  There are many analogies.

As far as I can tell, in the BATF's war on the Branch Davidians, they're
warring against the first two most important natural rights codified in
the US Constitution: freedom of religion, and the right to keep and bear
arms.

Dale made a casual comment about returning to the days when everyone
carried a handgun.  I was just reading a draft of an ISIL educational
pamphlet by Dave Kopel today on the crime rates of those days of the "Wild"
West: homicide rates were high for those that hung out at saloons, got
drunk, and got into fights, but all other crime rates were low.  Among
the rest of the people, homicide rates were low, too.  These rates were
less than one-tenth that of NYC today.  (BTW, since I just realized that
we now have at least two Dales who post, I was referring to Dale Owen
Rowley, not Dale Worley - their last names are even similar!)

Crime rates where handgun carrying is legal are lower than where it is not.
The essay was a bit over 1500 words, so I could go on and on.  Suffice to
say that if you value safety from crime, then you should encourage widespread
bearing of firearms in a responsible manner.

