Date: Wed, 3 Mar 1993 07:42:13 -0500 (EST)
From: Harry Shapiro <habs@Panix.Com>
Subject: Meta: Judgment

1. Judgment in Mr. Krieger vs. Mr. DeLancey

		and

2. Judgment in List Administration vs. Mr. Krieger

3. I have decided the forementioned cases. I have not previously
indicated to the list that I was seeking judgment against Mr.
Krieger. So I will first indicate what those charges are for. Then
I will explain why I am publishing both of these judgments together.
Finally I will present my judgments, which issue warnings to both
Mr. Krieger and Mr. DeLancey.

4. In my formal role of List Administrator I found that Mr. Krieger's
post to the list within which I announced that he was filing charges
against Mr. Delancey was in of itself inflammatory. Furthermore, list
rules (although unclear perhaps) forbid this type of post.

5. I am publishing my judgments on these two cases together because I
find that they are related, that they (the cases) illustrate how
charges should be made (and not made), the role of PPL on this list,
etc.

6. I find that Mr. DeLancey used communication that was inflammatory
and offensive. 

7. Mr. Delancey was very strongly sure that the facts he was presenting
represented a universal truism. It is not my desire to censure the
proclamation of "fact." Even using the methods of science it is
possible for "known" facts to later be proven wrong and often there is
room for disagreement.

8. The way and methods used by Mr. Delancey to declare his absolute
certainty of these facts, through the voice of his writing and Meta
communication contained within his posts left no room for reasonable
Extropians to disagree.

9. A more formal way of looking at the communication methods used by
Mr. Delancey is that in presenting his "facts" he used more "force"
of argument then was need to actually make his case.

10. Again the end result in either case is that Mr. Delancey inflamed,
and or posted what I call flame bait.

11. What is unresolved is how much or to what degree can a set of facts
can be declared in a post to this list as being the only "truth"
without violating the list rules. I will in future judgments look for
sincere politeness, a willingness to engage in reasonable debate, and
when adequate challenges are presented a willingness to either back down
or presented additional proof(s).

12. There are however, a set of Meta facts which are said to be certain
for list discussion: The ExI board and myself have by fiat declared
certain facts known as List Basics to be, for the purposes of list
discussions, to be "true;" more accurately we have declared these basic
facts to be in of themselves (as explained in previous judgments,
messages, etc.)  beyond debate. Our willingness to allow debates which
gets at the fine or often blurry points within the list basics mets
the critrea set in paragraph 12, for "declaration of truths."

13. In the case against Mr. Krieger, as in other cases, I have found
that those who seek a judgment often as a direct result find
themselves the subject of charges filed by the List Administrator. I
am worried that this in of itself will discourage list members from
seeking resolution under our PPL. Never-the-less, since legal
proceedings in of themselves are a force which can be used for
coercive means (e.g., give me what I want or I will sue), I must look
at and judge the entire situation, including how the charges were
made, how the defendant was notified of these charges, etc.

14. I find that I have been perhaps less then clear about how charges
should be made, presented etc. I will make this clearer. The publication
of this judgment is a part of that effort.

15. In simple terms: 	A) Make all charges directly to me
			B) I will notify all parties to the case
			C) I will make a post to the list:
				a) announcing the case
				b) freezing topics were needed
					(e.g., stopping flames)
			D) I will make and publish a judgment
			E) All judgments are open to appeal

16. A detail which I wish to bring forth is that "false" charges,
frivoulus complaints, etc. can result in the person making the
charge being found guilty of violating list rules.

17. Mr. Krieger followed step A as indicated in paragraph 15. At
the same time he notified Mr. Delancey which violates step B,
but since it was made through private communication is beyond by
purview.

18. Mr. Krieger discussed the case on the list in a way that did
violate steps B & C. He however did use the "Meta" prefix. This
same post, violated list rules against flaming and flame baiting.

19. I issue Mr. Delancey 1 out of 3 warnings for violations of list
rules.

20. I issue Mr. Krieger 1 out of 3 warnings for violations of list
rules.



